<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dantidurga</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 735–756</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dantidurga was the founder of the Rashtrakuta dynasty, ruling in the northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deccan">Deccan</a> from about 735 to 756. A feudatory of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chalukya-dynasty">Chalukyas</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/badami">Badami</a>, he overthrew his overlord <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kirtivarman-ii">Kirtivarman II</a> around 753 and made the Rashtrakutas the leading power of the Deccan. He was succeeded by his uncle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krishna">Krishna</a> I, who built the Kailasa temple at Ellora.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dantidurga.jpg" alt="Dantidurga" width="320" height="216" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Shraman revival · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rashtrakutas_Coins_25-07-23_15-44-48-445.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
